  "description": "ACIBEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H122 La6 O40 Ti1,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 9 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 8 O neighbors; La1A (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2A (La) has 9 O neighbors; Ti1A (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; La3A (La) has 8 O neighbors; La4? (La) has 0 O neighbors; La5? (La) has 0 O neighbors; La6? (La) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 0.687-4.263 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 13.70-128.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C68H122O40La6Ti. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
